<h1>Advanced Points vs Cash Calculator</h1>
<p class="sub">Stop comparing just the base numbers. This calculator factors in "hidden costs" like taxes and the points you would have earned by paying cash to give you a precise redemption verdict.</p>

<div class="panel">
  <div class="field">
    <label for="cashPrice">Cash ticket price<span class="hint" id="hintCash">$</span></label>
    <input type="number" id="cashPrice" value="500" min="0" step="1" inputmode="decimal" aria-describedby="hintCash">
  </div>
  
  <div class="row">
    <div class="field">
      <label for="pointsNeeded">Points or miles required<span class="hint" id="hintPoints">Points</span></label>
      <input type="number" id="pointsNeeded" value="40000" min="1" step="1" inputmode="numeric" aria-describedby="hintPoints">
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <label for="awardTaxes">Award taxes and surcharges<span class="hint" id="hintTaxes">$</span></label>
      <input type="number" id="awardTaxes" value="50" min="0" step="1" inputmode="decimal" aria-describedby="hintTaxes">
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="row">
    <div class="field">
      <label for="forgoneValue">Value of forgone points<span class="hint" id="hintForgone">$ (Optional)</span></label>
      <input type="number" id="forgoneValue" value="20" min="0" step="1" inputmode="decimal" aria-describedby="hintForgone unitForgone">
      <div class="unit" id="unitForgone">The value of points you would earn if you bought the cash ticket</div>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <label for="transferBonus">Transfer bonus<span class="hint" id="hintBonus">% (Optional)</span></label>
      <input type="number" id="transferBonus" value="0" min="0" step="1" inputmode="numeric" aria-describedby="hintBonus unitBonus">
      <div class="unit" id="unitBonus">E.g., enter 20 for a 20% transfer bonus</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="field">
    <label for="personalValuation">Personal point valuation<span class="hint" id="hintValuation">¢ / Point (Optional)</span></label>
    <input type="number" id="personalValuation" value="1.5" min="0" step="0.01" inputmode="decimal" aria-describedby="hintValuation unitValuation">
    <div class="unit" id="unitValuation">Your baseline expectation for how much a point is worth</div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="ticket" aria-live="polite">
  <div class="main">
    <div class="compare">
      <div class="item">
        <div class="k">Redemption Value (CPP)</div>
        <div class="v" id="cppResult" style="word-break: break-word; overflow-wrap: anywhere;">0.00¢ / point</div>
      </div>
      <div class="item">
        <div class="k">Equivalent Cost</div>
        <div class="v" id="costCompare" style="font-size:18px; margin-top:10px; word-break: break-word; overflow-wrap: anywhere;">Points Cost: -<br>Cash Cost: -</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="note" id="explain"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="perf"></div>
  <div class="stub">
    <div>
      <div class="verdict-label">Recommendation</div>
      <div class="verdict" id="verdictText">—</div>
    </div>
    <div class="code" id="verdictCode">DIFF —</div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="article-content prose" style="margin-top: 40px; padding-top: 40px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line);">
  <h2>Why Use an Advanced Calculator?</h2>
  <p>When deciding whether to use points or pay cash for an award ticket, simply comparing "points required" to the "cash ticket price" is often not enough. Real-world redemptions are full of "hidden costs". Our advanced calculator factors in four key variables to determine your True Cents Per Point (Actual CPP):</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>High Taxes and Surcharges:</strong> Some airlines (like British Airways or Emirates) charge exorbitant carrier-imposed surcharges on award tickets that can rival the cash price.</li>
    <li><strong>Forgone Points Value:</strong> If you pay cash for a flight, you earn frequent flyer miles and credit card points. When you redeem points, you "forgo" those earnings.</li>
    <li><strong>Transfer Bonuses:</strong> When banks offer a 20% or 30% bonus for transferring points to a specific airline, your actual point cost drops significantly.</li>
    <li><strong>Personal Valuation:</strong> Market values are just a baseline. This calculator lets you input your own personal valuation to see if the redemption meets your specific goals.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>The Advanced Formula</h3>
  <p>The advanced calculator uses a modified formula that accounts for these hidden variables:</p>
  <div class="formula-box">
    <span class="formula-name">Actual CPP =</span>
    <span class="formula-expression">(Cash Price - Award Taxes - Forgone Value) ÷ (Points Required ÷ (1 + Transfer Bonus %))</span>
  </div>

  <h3>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h3>
  <div class="faq">
    <details>
      <summary>What if the taxes are higher than the cash price?</summary>
      <div>
        <p>It is generally not recommended to use points for this redemption. If the taxes and fees equal or exceed the cash price of the ticket, consuming points rarely makes economic sense.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
    
    <details>
      <summary>How do I calculate "Forgone Value"?</summary>
      <div>
        <p>Imagine you would earn 10,000 miles if you paid cash for the ticket. If you personally value those miles at 1.0 cents each, your forgone value is $100. This amount should be subtracted from the cash price as a hidden cost of using points.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>What does the "DIFF" percentage mean?</summary>
      <div>
        <p>DIFF represents the percentage difference between the Actual CPP and your Personal Valuation. If it's positive (e.g., +20%), the redemption exceeded your expectations. If it's negative, it fell short.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>

